  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a hilly half marathon. By week six, the outside of the knee said nope, especially on the downhills. The internet's advice: roll that IT band. Ouch.\n\nOuter knee pain in runners is usually a load issue rather than a 'tight' band. The band barely changes length, so stretching or releasing it isn't the key.\n\nWhat often helps: temporarily cut long downhills and the distance that flares it, strengthen your hips, knees and calves, then rebuild distance, hills and uneven ground gradually. Foam rolling is fine for comfort, and cadence changes are best made after an assessment.\n\nPain that hangs around, big swelling, a fall or trouble walking normally is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
